    "body": "Depends on: #64. The current induced cover is 42 regions across 3 depths — far coarser than the 4×256 TLA class grid, which is one suspected cause of residual correlation and weak emissions. Sweep region budget (42 → 128 → 512) and split entropy threshold (0.25 → 0.1 bits) and measure reference top-1/top-M recall, frontier width, artifact bytes, and Gate C top-1 agreement under the fixed formula at each point. Acceptance: a rate-distortion table (regions × bytes × agreement) and a chosen operating point with the tradeoff documented; predictive_sufficiency module reused for the depth curves where applicable.\n\n\n---\n\n## Definition of Done\n- A rate-distortion sweep of the induced cover (≈42 → 128 → 512 regions; split threshold 0.25 → 0.1 bits) is measured under the fixed (#64) scorer.\n- An operating point (region budget + split threshold) is chosen and recorded with the tradeoff.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Each point reports: reference top-1/top-M recall, frontier width, artifact bytes, Gate C top-1 agreement.\n- [ ] Results are presented as a rate-distortion table (regions × bytes × agreement), deterministic double-run.\n- [ ] The chosen point is justified against the 42-region baseline row.",
